  "title": "A DFA that recognises multiples of three",
  "estimatedMinutes": 20,
  "instructions": "## Remainders as states\n\nThis machine reads a binary number from the most significant bit and accepts it when the number is divisible by 3. State **r0**, **r1** or **r2** is the remainder of the bits read so far. Reading bit b turns remainder r into (2r + b) mod 3.\n\n## Do this\n\n1. Step through the word **1101** (13 in decimal) and answer the questions.\n2. The questions about 110 and 1001 run those words for you; predict them by hand first.\n3. Then type your own word of **at least five symbols** that the machine accepts. Check it is a multiple of three in decimal.",
